Now the big game.js. Let me write it carefully, complete.

Structure:
1. Canvas setup
2. Game state
3. Screen management (menu/treasury/victory/defeat)
4. Wave management
5. Towers (placement, targeting, combat, animations)
6. Enemies update
7. Projectiles, particles
8. Base damage, win/lose
9. Rendering
10. Input
11. Loop init

Let me write it.

Key details to get right:
- `state` object.
- towerStats(t): returns dmg, range, fireRate, radius, windupDur, projectile.
- windup durations: archer 0.3, spear 0.25, mage 0.32, ballista 1.0 (reload).
- melee: projectile null → attack does instant damage at windup end; cooldown = fireRate after.
- ranged: projectile kind from type.

Tower attack flow:
```js
function tryAttack(t) {
  const ts = towerStats(t);
  if (t.state === "attack") return;
  const target = t.targetId != null ? findEnemy(t.targetId) : findTarget(t);
  if (target == null) { t.state = "idle"; t.targetId = null; return; }
  if (distTo(t, target) > ts.range) { t.state="idle"; t.targetId=null; return; }
  t.targetId = target.id;
  t.state = "attack";
  t.animT = 0;
  t.animDur = ts.windup;
  if (TOWER_TYPES[t.type].projectile === null) {
    // melee: resolve damage at end of swing
    pendingMelee = { tower: t, target: target, t: 0 };
  }
}
```

Hmm, simpler: handle in tower update:

```js
for (const t of state.towers) {
  const ts = towerStats(t);
  if (t.state === "attack") {
    t.animT += dt;
    if (t.animT >= t.animDur) {
      t.state = "idle";
      t.cooldown = ts.fireRate;
      const target = t.targetId != null ? findEnemy(t.targetId) : null;
      if (TOWER_TYPES[t.type].projectile === null) {
        if (target) doDamage(t, target);
      } else {
        if (target) {
          state.projectiles.push({ id: nextId(), towerId: t.id, kind: TOWER_TYPES[t.type].projectile, x: t.x, y: t.y, tx: target.x, ty: target.y, speed: projectileSpeed(kind), targetId: target.id, t: 0 });
        }
      }
    }
  } else {
    t.cooldown -= dt;
    if (t.cooldown <= 0) {
      // check target in range
      const target = t.targetId != null ? findEnemy(t.targetId) : findTarget(t);
      if (target) {
        const d = distTo(t, target);
        if (d <= ts.range) {
          t.state = "attack"; t.animT = 0; t.animDur = ts.windup;
          if (TOWER_TYPES[t.type].projectile === null) { doDamage(t, target); t.state="idle"; t.cooldown = ts.fireRate; }
        } else {
          t.cooldown = 0.05;
          t.state = "idle";
        }
      } else { t.state = "idle"; }
    }
  }
}
```

Wait, melee: when state idle and cooldown ready and target in range → set attack anim, then in attack update at end apply damage. Let me unify: both go through 'attack' state; ranged spawns projectile at windup end; melee applies damage at windup end.

```js
// in attack completion:
if (TOWER_TYPES[t.type].projectile === null) { const tg = t.targetId!=null?findEnemy(t.targetId):null; if (tg) doDamage(t, tg); }
else { spawn projectile at windup end toward target }
```

Good, consistent.

findEnemy(id): state.enemies.find(e => e.id === id).

Projectile speed: arrow 320, fire 260, bolt 240.

Projectile update:
```js
for (let i = state.projectiles.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
  const p = state.projectiles[i];
  const e = state.enemies.find(x => x.id === p.targetId);
  if (!e) { state.projectiles.splice(i,1); continue; }
  const d = Math.hypot(e.x - p.x, e.y - p.y);
  const sp = p.speed * dt;
  if (d <= sp) {
    // hit
    state.projectiles.splice(i, 1);
    doDamageByTowerId(p.towerId, e);
  } else {
    const s = sp / d;
    p.x += (e.x - p.x) * s;
    p.y += (e.y - p.y) * s;
    p.t += dt;
    if (p.t > 6) state.projectiles.splice(i, 1);
  }
}
```

doDamageByTowerId: find tower, doDamage.

doDamage(t, e): dmg = towerStats(t).dmg (includes level mult); e.hp -= dmg; e.flash = 0.15? (hit flash timer). If e.hp <= 0 → killEnemy(t, e).

killEnemy(t, e):
```js
state.kills++;
const reward = e.boss ? Math.round(e.gold * 5) : e.gold;
state.gold += reward;
spawnParticles(e.x, e.y, e.color);
// remove
state.enemies = state.enemies.filter(x => x !== e);
```

Wave cleared check in update after enemy updates.

Defeat check: state.baseHp <= 0 → endGame('defeat').

Win: wave === WORLD.MAX_WAVES && cleared → victory.

Wave clear → state.screen = 'between'.

**Wave flow details**: startGame(mapKey): reset: towers=[], enemies=[], projectiles=[], particles=[], gold=WORLD.GOLD_START, wave=0, kills=0, baseHp=WORLD.BASE_HP, spawnQueue=[], selectedTowerType=null, screen='playing'; wave=1; startWave(1).

startWave(w): state.wave = w; state.spawnQueue = buildWave(w); state.waveTimer = 0; state.screen = 'playing';

spawn handling in update:
```js
if (state.screen === "playing") {
  state.waveTimer -= dt;
  if (state.spawnQueue.length > 0) {
    if (state.waveTimer <= 0) {
      const tpl = state.spawnQueue[0];
      state.waveTimer = tpl.boss ? 2.5 : 0.85;
      spawnEnemy();
      state.waveTimer -= dt; // hmm
    }
  }
}
```
Cleaner: when waveTimer<=0 and queue nonempty → spawn tpl at front, pop, set timer.

```js
if (state.waveTimer <= 0 && state.spawnQueue.length) {
  const tpl = state.spawnQueue.shift();
  spawnEnemy(tpl);
  state.waveTimer = tpl.boss ? 2.6 : 0.8;
}
```

spawnEnemy(tpl): create enemy with stats from tpl + scaling; push; state.waveTimer handled above.

buildWave returns array of templates: {type, boss, hp, speed, dmg, gold, radius, color, dark}.

makeEnemy(tpl): enemy with path = deep copy of current map path, wi=0, etc.

reachedBase handling: in enemy update: `if (enemyStep(e, dt)) { breach: baseHp -= e.dmg; ... }`.

**Base**: baseHp in state; hearts drawn.

**Rendering**: write draw functions with ctx.

