RoundRect: use ctx.roundRect if available (modern browsers yes). Fallback: manual. Chrome supports roundRect now (2022+). Fine.

Grid: for gx 0..11, gy 0..15: strokeStyle "rgba(60,40,20,0.08)", line from (gx*40+0.5? ) — use lines at boundaries.

Draw placed towers: for t of state.towers: drawTower(t).

drawTower(t):
```js
const ts = towerStats(t);
const ty = TOWER_TYPES[t.type];
const size = 0.8 + 0.12*(t.level-1)? 
```
Tower visual size grows with level: scale = 0.85 + 0.12 * (t.level - 1). Hmm level 1 → 0.85, level 3 → 1.09. Let's do base 0.9 + 0.1*(level-1)? For visuals only.

Draw:
- shadow: ellipse at (x, y+10) rgba(0,0,0,0.2) rx size*radius.
- based on type.

I'll write drawing helpers:

drawArcher(t, ts, animT, animDur):
```
scale = ...;
// platform
circle fill ty.color dark? base: fillStyle ty.dark, arc(x, y+2, 12*scale, ...)
// legs: two lines color dark
// body: line shoulder->hip
// arm: shoulder (x, y-6) to hand; bow: line from (x, y-6) to (x + cos(handAng)*14?, ...). 
```
Simplify: character hangs from platform top (y - something). Tower at cell top area? Towers placed at cell center (x+20, y+20) typically on ground. Character base at ground y = t.y + 14 (platform height). Ugh.

Simplify: towers sit on "ground line" at y ≈ H-110 (ground top). Placement clamps cy such that tower within arena. Tower y = cell center; drawing treats bottom of tower at y + 16 (platform). Character stands at (x, y + 14).

